    "conclusion": "Plan B uniquely avoids violating any non-consensual stringent duty and provides the greatest permissible benefit; therefore the council should adopt Plan B.",
    "strongest_objection": "Plan C involves only consensual hardship and aids the single most exposed home, so benevolence should prioritize the worst-off individual.",
    "answer_to_objection": "Beneficence is outweighed when a markedly larger group (twelve households) can be helped at no rights-cost; the duty to aid the worst-off does not override equal moral claims of many others when no additional rights are at stake.",
    "reversal_condition": "Evidence that the twelve households face substantially lower risk than Jo—or that Sal’s hardship violates a separate duty despite consent—would reopen the comparison.",
    "residual_disagreement": []
